  "term": "concrete operational stage",
  "definition": "The concrete operational stage is described here as a developmental period, usually around ages 7 to 11, when children are thought to be especially ready to learn logical structures and algorithmic reasoning. In this source, it is presented as an important window for building problem-solving and early abstract thinking through activities such as coding.",
